{"id":"word:hebrew:H6031","type":"word","title":"עָנָה","subtitle":"H6031 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to depress literally or figuratively, transitive or intransitive (in various applications, as follows)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to עָנָה (H6031) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 83 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"עָנָה (ʻânâh) means to depress literally or figuratively, transitive or intransitive (in various applications, as follows) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 2 26."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"עָנָה","transliteration":"ʻânâh","pronunciation":"aw-naw'","strong":"H6031","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6031","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וְ/עִנִּיתֶ֖ם","תַעֲנֵֽ/ם","לְ/עַנּוֹת֔/וֹ","עִנָּ֖ה","לַ/עֲנ֥וֹת"],"morphs":[["HVpp3ms",5],["HVpp3cp",4],["HC/Vpq2mp",4],["HR/Vpc/Sp3ms",3],["HVhi2ms/Sp3mp",2],["HC/Vpw3ms/Sp3fs",2],["HVpc/Sp3ms",2],["HVpc/Sp2ms",2],["HR/Vqc",2],["HVpi3mp",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to depress literally or figuratively, transitive or intransitive (in various applications, as follows)","usage":"abase self, afflict(-ion, self), answer (by mistake for 6030 ), chasten self, deal hardly with, defile, exercise, force, gentleness, humble (self), hurt, ravish, sing (by mistake for 6030 ), speak (by mistake for 6030 ), submit self, weaken, × in any wise.","full":"H6031. anah II. [ עָנָה ] verb be occupied, busied with ( ב ), only Ecclesiastes (perhaps Aramaic loan-word; Syriac be occupied with , occupation, affair ; compare Arabic , concern one , also be occupied by; Ecclus 42:8 margin); — Qal Infinitive עֲנוֺתִ Eccl 1:13 ; 3:10 . III. [ עָנָה ] verb be bowed down, afflicted ( Late Hebrew id. ; MI Pi`el ויענו Psa 1:5 , אענו 1:6 ; Assyrian enû thwart, frustrate, do violence to ; Arabic , be lowly subsmissive , see Rahlfs עָנִי und עָנָי in d. Psalmen (1892), 67 ff. ; עַנִּי ᵑ7 Pa`el oppress ; Syriac Ethpe`el humble oneself , and derivatives); — Qal Perfect 1singular עָנִיתִי 116:10 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular יַעֲנֶה Isa 25:5 ; 31:4 , etc.; &#8212; 1 be put down or become low , of song of triumph Isa 25:5 (others as Hiph`il he putteth down , || תַּכְנִיעַ ). 2 be depressed, downcast Isa 31:4 (of lion; || יֵחָ֑ת ). 3 be afficted Psa 116:10 ; 119:67 ; Zech 10:2 . Niph`al Perfect 1singular נַעֲניתִי Psa 119:107 ; Infinitive construct לֵעָנֹת (perhaps read as Qal Ges § 51 l ) Exod 10:3 ; Participle נַעֲנֶה Isa 53:7 ; feminine singular נַעֲנָה 58:10 ; &#8212; 1 humble oneself מִמְּנֵי Exod 10:3 . 2 be afficted Psa 119:107 ; Isa 53:7 ; 58:10 . Piel. Perfect 3masculine singular עִנָּה Deut 22:24 5 t.; 2 masculine singular עִנִּיתָ Psa 88:8 ; 1 singular עִנֵּיתִי 35:13 , suffix וְעִנִּתִךְ consecutive Nahum 1:12 , etc.; Imperfect יְעַנֶּה Job 37:23 , etc.; Imperative עַנּוּ Judg 19:24 ; Infinitive absolute עַנֵּה Exod 22:22 ; construct עַנּוֺת Isa 58:5 +, etc.; Participle plural suffix מְעַנַּיִךְ 60:14 ; Zeph 3:19 ; &#8212; 1 humble, mishandle, afflict: individual Gen 16:6 ; 31:50 (J) Exod 22:21 ; 22:22 (twice in verse) (E) Job 30:11 ; by imprisonment and bonds Judg 16:5-6 , 19 ; Psa 105:18 ; a nation by war or in bondage Gen 15:13 (J) Exod 1:11-12 , Num 24:24 (twice in verse) (E) Deut 26:6 ; 1Sam 12:8 (inserting מִצְרַיִם וַיְעַנּוּם , so ᵐ5 Dr Bu Kit HPS [compare Th We]), 2Sam 7:10 ; 2Kin 17:20 ; Psa 94:5 ; Isa 60:14 ; Zeph 3:19 ; dynasty of David Psa 89:23 . 2 humble , a woman by cohabitation, Gen 34:2 (J) Deut 21:14 ; 22:24 , 29 ; Judg 19:24 ; 20:5 ; 2Sam 13:12 , 14 , 22 , 32 ; Ezek 22:10-11 , Lam 5:11 . 3 afflict as a discipline (God agent) Deut 8:2-3 , 16 ; 1Kin 11:39 ; Psa 88:8 ; 90:15 ; 119:75 ; Isa 64:11 ; Nahum 1:12 (twice in verse); Lam 3:33 . 4 humble, weaken , object כֹּחַ Psa 102:24 ; משׁפט Job 37:23 (compare Talmud דִּין עִנָּה ); נֶפֶשׁ oneself , by fasting Lev 16:29 , 31 ; 23:27 , 32 ; Num 29:7 (P) Psa 35:13 ; Isa 58:3 , 5 ; by an oath Num 30:14 (P). Pu`al Perfect 1singular עֻנֵּיתִי Psa 119:71 ; Imperfect 3feminine singular תְּעֻנֶּה Lev 23:29 ; Infinitive construct suffix עֻנּוֺתוֺ Psa 132:1 ; Participle מְעֻנֶּה Isa 53:4 ; &#8212; 1 be afflicted , in discipline by God Psa 119:71 ; 132:1 ; Isa 53:4 . 2 be humbled by fasting Lev 23:29 (P). Hiph`il Imperfect 2masculine singular suffix תַּעֲנֵם 1Kin 8:35 2Chr 6:26 afflict , in discipline. Hithpa`el Perfect 3masculine singular הִתְעַנָּה 1Kin 2:26 ; 2 masculine singular תִתְעַנִּיתָ 2:26 ; Imperfect 3masculine plural יִתְעַנּוּ Psa 107:17 ; Imperative הִתְעַנִּי Gen 16:9 ; Infinitive construct הִתְעַנּוֺת Ezekiel 8:21; Dan 10:12 ; &#8212; 1 humble oneself (with יָדֶיהָ תַּחַת ) Gen 16:9 (J). 2 be afflicted , by men 1Kin 2:26 (twice in verse); by God in discipline Psa 107:17 . 3 humble oneself in fasting Ezra 8:21 ; Dan 10:12 . II. ענה (√ of following; see Biblical Hebrew III. עָנִי עָנָו, ענה, ).","rootNote":"a primitive root (possibly rather identical with 6030 through the idea of looking down or browbeating);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 2 26","keyReferences":["1Kgs 2 26","1Kgs 2 26","1Kgs 8 35","1Kgs 11 39","2Chr 6 26","2Kgs 17 20","2Sam 7 10","2Sam 13 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":83,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 2 26","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִתְעַנִּ֔יתָ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtp2ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 26","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הִתְעַנָּ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVtp3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 8 35","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":35,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תַעֲנֵֽ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhi2ms/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 39","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/אעַנֶּ֛ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpi1cs"},{"reference":"2Chr 6 26","book":"2Chr","chapter":